    },
    {
     "type": "MTEXT",
     "text": "{\\L\\C256;NOTES:\\l\\P\\P\\pi-0.26,l0.26,t0.26;1.^IALL BIORETENTION FACILITIES SHALL HAVE A MINIMUM 20 FOOT ACCESS EASEMENT CONNECTING TO A DEDICATED PUBLIC RIGHT OF WAY.  ACCESS ROAD SHALL HAVE MIN. 12' STABILIZED WIDTH, MAX. LONG. GRADE OF 15%, MAX. CROSS-SLOPE 5%. \\H1.116x;IN ADDITION, A 10-FOOT WIDE PERMANENT MAINTENANCE ACCESS EASEMENT MUST BE PROVIDED AROUND THE PERIMETER OF ALL BMPS TO ALLOW FOR ADEQUATE MAINTENANCE AND REPAIR.\\P\\pi0,l0,tz;\\H0.8961x;\\P\\pi-0.26,l0.26,t0.26;2.^IALL DRAINAGE AREAS TO A BIORETENTION  FACILITY ARE TO BE STABILIZED PRIOR TO  INSTALLATION OF AMENDED SOILS, MULCH OR PLANTINGS. \\P\\pi0,l0,tz;\\P\\pi-0.26,l0.26,t0.26;3.^IAMENDED SOIL WILL ONLY BE PERMITTED WITH A VALID SOIL ANALYSIS REPORT. NO AMENDED SOIL SHALL BE ALLOWED ON THE SIDE SLOPES.\\P\\pi0,l0,tz;\\P\\pi-0.26,l0.26,t0.26;4.^IINSTALL WIRE SCREENING AROUND ALL OUTLET OPENINGS TO PREVENT LOSS OF MULCH.\\P\\pi0,l0,tz;\\P\\pi-0.26,l0.26,t0.26;5.^IUNDERDRAIN PIPE SHOULD BE MIN. 6\" PERFORATED SCHEDULE 40 PVC (PER AASHTO M278) OR DOUBLE WALL HDPE (PER AASHTO M252).   PERFORATIONS SHOULD BE 3/8\" SPACED 3\" ON CENTER ALONG 4 LONGITUDINAL ROWS SPACED 90\u00b0 APART.\\P\\pi0,l0,tz;\\P\\pi-0.26,l0.26,t0.26;6.^IUNDERDRAIN CLEANOUTS SHOULD EXTEND A MIN. OF 6\" ABOVE MAXIMUM PONDING ELEVATION. ONE CLEANOUT MAY BE FLUSH WITH TOP OF SURFACE TO ALLOW DRAWDOWN.  \\P\\pi0,l0,tz;\\P\\pi-0.225,l0.225;7.  ONLY SMALL MATURING TREES ARE ALLOWED TO BE PLANTED IN THE AMENDED SOILS.}",
